                <pb facs="0677" n="645" xml:id="pg645"/>

                <head>363. Memorandum of a Conversation Between the President and the Secretary of
                    State, Washington, August 21, 1957, 11:30 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d363-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1957-08-21T11:30:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 21, 1957, 11:30
                        a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Syria</hi></p>
                <p>I said I was much concerned about the situation. I felt that unless there was
                    some reaction the consequences might be very serious indeed. The neighbors of
                    Syria were all much concerned and it was a good time to mobilize that sentiment.
                    All in turn were watching what the United States thought. I said that we planned
                    a meeting at the State Department at 2:30 and I would report to him fully after
                    that. I said that General Goodpaster
                    would be present. The President suggested that John Eisenhower also be present.</p>
                <p>The President agreed with my estimate and threw out the suggestion that we might
                    give arms and money rather freely to Syria’s neighbors as part of some
                    program.</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion concerning disarmament and China.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >JFD</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
